offenders by age group).\n\n## Important caveats\n- These are several different counts (police cases, gendarmerie cases, court cases) that overlap and are not additive. Police and gendarmerie cover different territories (towns vs. rural areas). The measure column names the agency and the stage.\n- The legal categories differ: \"assassinat\" (premeditated murder), \"meurtre\" (murder), \"homicide volontaire\", \"coups mortels\" (fatal assault), \"homicide involontaire\" (negligent). All kept as published.\n- 2022 legion figures (Tableau 12-4) are published by month; only the published \"Totaux\" column is a row value, and the 12 monthly values are listed in the note.\n- Centre Tableau 11-1: in the PDF text the 2021 column headers are garbled; I assumed the same order as 2018-2019 (majeurs, mineurs, total, nombre de cas), which fits the numbers (75 + 4 = 79).\n- Littoral Tableau 12-2 values for Douala are 0 in both years. That is gendarmerie only; Douala city homicides are policed by the Sûreté Nationale.\n\n## Not extracted (exists, not done in this run)\nINS publishes a statistical yearbook for each of the 10 regions, several editions each (list via https://ins-cameroun.cm/?s=annuaire+statistique and the WordPress media data service https://ins-cameroun.cm/wp-json/wp/v2/media?search=annuaire). Each has a Justice and/or Sécurité chapter, but the table layouts differ between regions and editions. Not opened or extracted: Adamaoua (2024, 2025), Ouest (2021, 2022, 2024), Nord-Ouest (2022, 2023, 2024), Sud-Ouest (2023), Nord (2019), Littoral (2015, 2019, 2021, 2022, 2023 editions), Centre (earlier editions), Est, Extrême-Nord and Sud (none seen in the listing). Doing them all needs a table-by-table parser for each one. Earlier Littoral editions probably repeat the same series for earlier years.\n- National \"Annuaire Statistique du Cameroun, édition 2019\": the main PDF (ANNUAIRE_STATISTIQUE_EDITION_2019_PUBLIE.pdf) downloaded as only 43 KB (truncated or not a PDF); its post page lists no chapter files. The national yearbook's justice/security chapter was not checked.\n- The DGSN (police) and the gendarmerie do not publish national reports by region online, as far as I found. The Ministry of Health / DHIS2 public dashboard (https://ins-cameroun.cm/dashbord-public-des-statistiques-de-la-sante/) was not checked for assault deaths.","unmatched":12,"shapes":{"shapes_ADM1.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen CMR ADM1","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/CMR/ADM1/geoBoundaries-CMR-ADM1.geojson","licence":"Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 License","year":"2016"},"shapes_ADM2.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen CMR ADM2","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/CMR/ADM2/geoBoundaries-CMR-ADM2.geojson","licence":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)","year":"2016"}}}